/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-core-problem-chatgpt-package-20260908/package-r6/02-GLOBAL-VIEWS.md:5:Context. A multi-user LEO handover RL system deploys a per-user decision `a_u* = masked argmax_a [Q1_u(a) + Q2_u(a) + z3_u(a)/κ]` (28 slots, 100 users, one central scheduler per 30.08 s interval). Q1 (228-D "C1") predicts each user's one-step handover surplus in bits minus λ·(network-energy delta); Q2 (448-D "C2", OPS-3) prices persistence/service risk over future offsets; the third head "C3" was meant to capture what one user's choice does to everyone else (interference, shared PA supply, beam activation/circuit/baseband charges, bandwidth sharing) — the "load balance / coordination" term. The scientific objective is pooled network energy efficiency EE = Σbits / Σjoules over matched TRAIN anchors with a served-fraction margin of 0.001 versus BASE = argmax(Q1+Q2). Over 09-01 → 09-07, eighteen attempts across eight C3 target families all failed to raise pooled EE with a deployable target; the striking facts are that even EXACT oracle labels composed through the additive per-user rule LOST EE (MONE −2.64%, 3/3 lineages; PNFE −11.1%; unilateral surpluses positive in 60/60 diagnostics while the realised joint direction reversed in 28), the only positive family (ZR +0.94–0.98%) depended on realised fading that no deployable policy sees (EXPECTED_ZR fast screen → STOP), the pairwise coalition test R7 gave −0.049% pooled (2/8 worlds positive), and the cost-share targets D/F gave −1.33% / −4.54% with service failing. The owner's question: "the low confidence must be about the current overall design, mainly the C3 target formula (r3); C1's EE formula is fixed and C2 has little influence — or are there other big influences? Load balance should be directly related to EE; how can it be impossible to find a way to improve EE? That seems unreasonable."
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-core-problem-chatgpt-package-20260908/package-r6/02-GLOBAL-VIEWS.md:6:Answer, with evidence: (a) Is the load-balance ↔ EE intuition right in THIS simulator's energy model? Where does rebalancing gain bits versus cost joules (PA efficiency curve, saturation, activation/circuit/baseband charges, bandwidth sharing, path loss to farther satellites)? Under what regime would rebalancing pay, and does the record show whether the evaluated worlds are in it? (b) Decompose the levers and say which is binding by evidence: (1) the C3 target formula/label, (2) the composition rule (independent per-user additive argmax; never varied except a tie-breaker draft), (3) the deployable information interface (no realised fading; no others' same-slot actions), (4) the decision horizon (one-step vs adaptive trajectory), (5) the objective/evaluation (ratio of sums + service margin; BASE already prices energy through C1; matched-anchor pooled EE), (6) the physical regime (100 users / 28 slots / field keys; no favourable-regime selection allowed), (7) BASE's strength itself (how much first-order EE Q1+Q2 already captures). (c) If you were free to redesign globally (not bound to "a third additive head"), what would you build to convert coordination into pooled EE — e.g. a set-level/joint decoder, C3 as a scheduler/constraint (beam evacuation, admission, activation budgeting), a different decomposition of the objective, or a different BASE — and which of those are admissible PRE-OUTCOME under the integrity rules (no tuning against observed results; declared mechanism/interface/formula/deployment/panel/falsifier; no TEST)? (d) The existence screen E1 is running now: U₁ = exact certified best pooled EE with at most one changed user per anchor (Dinkelbach + exact DP, service-constrained) and J₁ = the best over a fixed joint "evacuate one origin beam" catalog. State what each of the four outcome cells would mean for the owner's intuition and for the redesign options. (e) Give an honest, probability-free statement: what can realistically be done within days versus what is a follow-up paper, and what single experiment after E1 would be most informative.
