/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-v1-chatgpt-package-20260908/package-r5/03-ASTRA-ROUND1-INVENTORY.md:119:**Mechanism:** legacy rewards include \(r_1=R_u/P^N\), \(r_2=-\Phi\), and \(r_3=-U_b\), with normalization, weights and temporal accumulation. Summed \(r_3=-\sum_b U_b^2\) favors spreading, while the energy model can favor consolidation. Summing or discounting per-step EE also differs from pooled EE. **Exploiters:** legacy learners face these trade-offs; endpoint search does not. **Magnitude:** potentially substantial for genuinely legacy-trained comparisons, but **the Φ-trained-BASE explanation is unsupported for C3-S’s authenticated repriced Q1/Q2 heads**. Their active objectives are B09. **Status:** DECLARED legacy terms; checkpoint attribution must be corrected. **Handle: FIX the explanatory record; DECLARE the objective separately for every sealed experiment.** [step.py:1051](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/step.py:1051), [service.py:264](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/service.py:264), [authority.json:11](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/.scratch/multi-catfish-v020-c3-source-audit/repriced-q1-q2-fit/lineage-2026092101/authority.json:11), [EVIDENCE-02:70](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-physics/EVIDENCE-02-HARNESS-AUDIT-OPUS.md:70)
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/HANDOFF-EXECUTION-CLOSURE-AUDIT-2026-09-07.md:516:- **Derivation (verified against `r7_balanced_successor_gate.py:adjudicate_section14_r7`).** Precedence: integrity → pair_coverage → (mechanics ∧ physical_signature ∧ teacher_composition) → (target_support ∧ held_out_learner ∧ world_stability) → (action_exposure ∧ literal_11 ∧ harmful_partial ∧ topology_consistency ∧ learned_composition ∧ service) → GO. `physical_signature=false` decides the token: pooled ratio-of-sums EE of the 11 profile versus 00 is −0.049% (`pooled_joint_direction=-1`) and only 2 of 8 worlds are positive (threshold: strictly positive and ≥4). `mechanics` (688/688) and `teacher_composition` (+0.335% vs baseline, 5 worlds) passed. Also false at lower precedence: `learned_composition` (−0.660% vs baseline, 2 worlds), `topology_consistency` (379/707 = 0.536 < 0.8), `harmful_partial` (`verify_v023_lcsrs_final.py:1668` — predicate true only when the harmful-partial fraction ≤ 0.05; it is false). Had physics passed, the token would have been `REDESIGN_INTERFACE_R7`, not GO. Held-out learner (balanced accuracy 0.705 vs placebo 0.626, spearman 0.839, 8/8 world wins), world stability, C1/C2 context all passed.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/HANDOFF-EXECUTION-CLOSURE-AUDIT-2026-09-07.md:652:- **Owner's question ("isn't the low confidence mainly about the r3 formula? load balance should be directly related to EE") answered by two independent global-view examinations** (`GLOBAL-VIEW-C3-QUESTION-2026-09-08.md`; astra ultra `GLOBAL-VIEW-C3-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-…`; Gemini 3.8 Flash High `GLOBAL-VIEW-C3-GEMINI-3.8-FLASH-HIGH-…`). Converging findings: (1) the C3 target formula is NOT the binding lever — exact oracle labels composed through the independent per-user additive argmax lost pooled EE; MONE's unilateral predicted gains were cancelled 97 % by the interaction residual; (2) the composition rule is the primary bottleneck, the deployable information interface second, BASE strength third; (3) physics: per-beam RF power is the max over served users, legal power (≤ 1.65 W) is far below PA saturation (5.218 W) so there is no congestion-driven PA penalty; PA ≈ 94.8 % of total power, so savings come from closing whole beams (+0.338 W circuit; new satellite +0.2 W baseband); same-beam users share 166.667 MHz so head-counts cancel in total rate — "spreading load" costs joules faster than it earns bits, which the record confirms (MONE bits +5.4 % / joules +8.2 %; F1 D +6.9/+8.4 %, F +14.7/+20.2 %; R7 consolidation −2.2 % / −2.1 %); (4) redesign, if pursued, is a set-level scheduler with a joint decoder (Q3 need not be a third additive head), admissible only as a separate pre-outcome contract; (5) the most informative single experiment after E1: astra — a deployable-information decoder kill screen (BASE vs privileged oracle vs deployable set-level scheduler); Gemini — decode E1's optimal profiles through the additive argmax to test whether partial adoption self-destroys the gain (minutes of compute).
