/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-10. Commissioned as a design consultation to `gpt-6-astra` at ultra effort and to `claude-fable-5-1`, both given the same neutral prompt that did not state my position. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing was run; nothing sealed was modified. Related: [additive split], [pair insufficiency], [novelty closed].
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ACCOUNTABILITY-WHY-NOT-SOONER-2026-09-10.md:5:A sequence of **pre-registered gates**, each of which genuinely failed, and each of which the contract's own rules then used to prohibit advancing: the physics gate whose eleven-against-zero-zero pooled efficiency came out at −0.049 % with two of eight worlds positive, ending that successor route under §7; the fast kill screen that returned no support and barred the next two stages; and earlier three-head, context and reference-gate failures.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ACCOUNTABILITY-WHY-NOT-SOONER-2026-09-10.md:11:- the sealed provisioning credits nothing on about three quarters of transmission instances and attains the per-user rate target for **none** of two thousand users, so the gates that failed were measured on a model in that state;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-EVAL-DATE-POOL-2026-09-09.md:5:The executable ephemeris split is a 16-day cycle from 2025-07-27: **7 days TRAIN, 1 embargo, 7 days TEST, 1 embargo**. The code defines `TRAIN`, `TEST` and a non-sampling `EMBARGO`, and the provider is fail-closed against TEST starts and TEST file reads. The embargo day means a TRAIN start's element window cannot reach a TEST date.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-EVAL-DATE-POOL-2026-09-09.md:26:**B. Use TEST as the evaluation pool.** Clean by construction and already enforced fail-closed. But it directly contradicts the sealed non-negotiable, and it spends the held-out set on an experiment that is not the final claim.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:6:**Stop the six-arm, many-seed success panel.** *Accept.* Six arms and many learner seeds ahead of one useful learned decision procedure is expensive rehearsal of an unanswered question. Nothing is being run on that path today.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:8:**Stop growing the corpus toward 51k–93k labels on the strength of an extrapolated curve.** *Accept, with the reason restated.* The decisive observation is not the extrapolation, it is that at the largest measured point the head still loses on both regret and realised efficiency — 10.3098 against 10.3178 Mbit/J — while its exact-best frequency improves. More accurate values have not yet produced a better rule. Growth resumes only if a measurement shows accuracy converting into decisions.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:10:**Stop treating a larger timeout or faster certification as the fix for the unilateral comparator.** *Accept.* The profiling shows genuinely late winners, 41 to 86 improving iterations and a longest uncensored run of 1,213 s. The tail is real work, not proof overhead. The two-arm split — offline certification for diagnosis, a separately declared anytime comparator for evaluation — is already required by contract v1.2 item 6, so this is not a new gate.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:12:**Stop sweeping the disputed circuit constant as a rescue.** *Accept.* The fixed-assignment sensitivity already answered whether that constant creates the sign; it does not, and the effect is larger at zero watts. More points do not address the real objection.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:14:**Stop broad defect adjudication as the default activity.** *Accept in principle, and I am the one who has been violating it.* Repair only what the selected result needs.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:16:**Stop rebuilding the first two heads merely to preserve the three-component story.** *Reject, on the owner's standing requirement.* The review is right that the mechanism study does not need them, and right that repairing two surrogates to protect a narrative is bad science. But the owner's requirement is not narrative: each of the three components must genuinely raise pooled efficiency, and publishing a negative for one of them is explicitly not acceptable. The sufficiency diagnostic has since shown that on the current encoders the first head has held-out explained variance of −0.336 — worse than predicting the mean — with a proved collision that no deterministic predictor can escape. Under that defect a three-head run cannot be a fair test of the first two, and a null from it would be uninterpretable. So the encoder repair is a **precondition for answering the owner's question at all**, not a rescue of a story. It stays. The review did not have this requirement in front of it.
